             no T16/T32 pair in the sweep -- the full-sweep CV flatters BOTH rules,
             because at small T they select nearly the same depths.  EXTEND the sweep upward (--T 8 16 32 64) so a second uncensored point exists.

  THE TWO CRITERIA DO NOT AGREE: magnitude UNRELIABLE (edge re-crosses the floor), novelty ABSOLUTE.
  magnitude says how much the state still moves; novelty says whether the
  movement is anywhere NEW.  PREFER NOVELTY when they part -- Z carries the
  pathway, not the displacement.

  MAGNITUDE IS UNRELIABLE at T=[32]: the series RE-CROSSES its floor, so
  its edge is a LAST crossing and grows with the OBSERVATION WINDOW rather than
  with the band.  That defect hands the verdict to RELATIVE by construction:
  a longer sweep catches one more excursion above the floor and the edge moves
  with T for a reason that has nothing to do with where the information is.
  Read the first-run edge instead, or move the floor clear of the oscillation.

